# TS2578 ("Unused '@ts-expect-error' directive") is not implemented. The
# suppression half of `@ts-expect-error` is; the unused report is not, because
# it is only sound on a checker that reports everything the oracle does. ztsc
# deliberately under-reports in places, so a directive the oracle considers used
# can look unused here, and TS2578 on that basis would be a false positive on
# correct code — the one thing project policy forbids. Deterministic
# under-report of a whole check.
directives/012_ts_expect_error_unused.ts  -TS2578 7

# The callback-parameter relation is ADDITIVE in ztsc, where tsc makes it the
# only test for a pair of single-call-signature parameters. When the callback
# comparison fails, ztsc falls back to the pre-existing
# contravariant/bivariant parameter check instead of rejecting, so the two
# directions tsc rejects *because* the callback relation is exclusive are
# under-reported: a method callback related in the contravariant direction
# (line 25), and a callback nested one level deeper, which tsc relates
# strictly (line 74). Made exclusive, the rule also rejects pairs
# whole-signature bivariance accepted, and every such case measured across the
# 16-package corpus was an unrelated inference gap surfacing
# (`Observable<unknown>` where tsc infers `Observable<number>`) — i.e. it would
# trade this fix for a batch of false positives, which policy forbids. The 7
# positives in the same case prove the relation itself is in place.
assignability/065_callback_parameter_variance.ts  -TS2322 25
assignability/065_callback_parameter_variance.ts  -TS2322 74

# A rest parameter typed by a UNION is modelled per POSITION at a CALL: each
# argument position gets the union of the constituents' element types (tsc's
# `getIndexedAccessType(restType, number)`), widened by `undefined` where some
# constituent makes the position optional. That is what contextually types a
# callback argument and what accepts an optional options bag. tsc additionally
# relates the argument list *as a whole* to the rest type
# (`getSignatureApplicabilityError` does zero positional checks once
# `getNonArrayRestType` answers), so it rejects a list that mixes constituents:
# a bare handler and an array of handlers in one call (041), an options bag in
# the defaultValue slot (053). ztsc accepts those — a deterministic under-report
# of one extra check.
#
# Its SIGNATURE-RELATION half is implemented (`sigRestUnion` /
# `restTupleAtPosition`, conformance calls/053), where whole-list arm choice is
# what an assignment actually turns on. The call half additionally needs `const`
# type parameters (tsc's `isConstTypeVariable` puts a template-literal argument
# written for a `const Key extends …` rest arm in a const context, so it keeps
# its literal type); without them the whole-list check rejects `t(`P.${x}`)` at
# every i18next call site, i.e. it would trade this under-report for a batch of
# false positives, which policy forbids.
#
# 041: the per-position check still discriminates — an incompatible callback is
# rejected on line 31.
calls/041_rest_param_union_of_arrays.ts  -TS2345 27
calls/053_rest_param_union_of_tuples.ts  -TS2345 58

# A cast whose source or target is a DEFERRED indexed access (`T[K]`) is
# conceded outright (indexed/031): tsc rejects one only when
# `getBaseConstraintOfType` fully reduces the access, which needs the object
# constraint to answer for every key the index constraint admits. Reducing it
# structurally instead — substituting each parameter's constraint — also
# collapses the shapes tsc leaves deferred, and then rejects casts tsc accepts
# (`s as T[K]` under `T extends { a: number; b: number }`, plus four more in
# 031). Trading one deterministic under-report for five false rejections is the
# standing policy direction. Line 14, whose operands are not deferred, still
# reports.
indexed/032_cast_to_deferred_indexed_access_negatives.ts  -TS2352 8


